# No Cursor text in git commits

Never add Cursor, Cursor Agent, Cursor Cowork, or any AI/tool attribution to git.

## Commit messages

- Write only a normal subject/body.
- Do not mention Cursor, Copilot, or that an agent wrote the code.
- Do not use `git commit --trailer`.
- Do not add any of these:
  - `Co-authored-by: Cursor`
  - `Co-authored-by: ... cursoragent@cursor.com`
  - `Made-with: Cursor`
  - `Made with Cursor`

## If a trailer is injected anyway

Strip it before finishing. Amend only when that commit is still local, created in this session, and not pushed. Otherwise make a new clean commit with no trailer.

```
# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "Add empty app." --trailer "Co-authored-by: Cursor"

# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "Add empty app."
```
